a1b","maturity":"draft","page_type":"entity","path":"pages/entities/vibepod-vibepod-cli-9b2c4f079a1b.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":[],"title":"vibepod/vibepod-cli","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:21:45Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4c9aa1a94916442b9ede63ee46a01d22"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_50c0ee0bbe48c244d12500bef316e64c8af9e08294af86c2221cad6b6bad446c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the test runner is pytest (`python -m pytest`); CI also validates default images with `scripts/check_default_images.py`, and `ruff check`, `ruff format --check`, and `mypy` are pre-commit gated. Tests should run with a throwaway `VP_CONFIG_DIR` when a host global config exists."}],"claim_ids":["clm_50c0ee0bbe48c244d12500bef316e64c8af9e08294af86c2221cad6b6bad446c"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:21:45Z","created_by_operation":"op_4c9aa1a94916442b9ede63ee46a01d22","id":"pg_b0f72494a29e5f6cbcf8aa41d1d15c23","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/vibepod-vibepod-cli-agents-md-ef6519007b1d-aa41d1d15c23.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_5042c1b39a10567681570fd1c89eb99e"],"title":"VibePod/vibepod-cli/AGENTS.md @ ef6519007b1d","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:21:45Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4c9aa1a94916442b9ede63ee46a01d22"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_3dbcc01d27a7595931ef4e502a5001acfd59a66f9f972c02f0033bfc42a88a7e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Each agent runs in its own Docker or Podman container, with default images published under the `vibepod` namespace on Docker Hub (e.g. `vibepod/claude:latest`, `vibepod/codex:latest`)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4159193229c12321477102e459493848f58508a800d2f989df15964f27e1c450"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Metrics are collected locally while agents run and served through a built-in dashboard managed via `vp logs start/stop/status`, showing per-agent HTTP traffic, usage over time, and Claude token metrics."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5835348860345d9d0d91ce0e68f0d4f6378517660cfe16d6ca8f8bbde6244210"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project describes itself as privacy-first: all metrics are collected and stored locally and never sent to the cloud."},{"claim_ids":["clm_65cc574b85b2d8a5f9efa36f1c855bda2b1ab476aa5abfcf379e73838cbb5b5a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"`--ikwid` appends each agent's auto-approval/permission-skip flag when supported; e.g. claude gets `--dangerously-skip-permissions`, gemini and qwen get `--approval-mode=yolo`, and several agents (opencode, auggie, tau, jcode, freebuff, dsh) are listed as not supported."},{"claim_ids":["clm_718605621670a3b371a48d654c4c4b2de63b573a603ad07da77607bb1ae4162f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI is installable via pip (`pip install vibepod`), Homebrew, and conda-forge (conda, mamba, pixi)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8ebe4a6ab137885c1e9b9ff564cfee3a0418039e0220a972aac6dfa2e0d88600"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Project overlays let users commit a FROM-less Dockerfile fragment in `.vibepod/overlay/`; VibePod auto-builds a cached, content-addressed image layer on top of the agent's base image."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a5c4ffb79a0645efc9a4f803666364306864eaba630392c31d9710da2edf9363"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"`vp run <agent> --acp` turns the CLI into an Agent Client Protocol adapter so the containerized agent appears in ACP-capable editors like Zed, with isolation, profiles, overlays and proxy metrics intact."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b6ec1f0db41fcf1a048564c6adca0287e2245852b103ad24e02b9f1a8f76037a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Reusable prompt recipes ('skills') can be installed per-project or per-user with `vp skills add`."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e571f591456707e025b6162ad43133b5cb9107c0f1256c63a64c83faadb4b670"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Implemented v1 commands include `vp run`, `vp stop <agent|--all>`, `vp list`, `vp config init/show/path`, and `vp version`."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e91eaa48f1a08e42e542895ab9a6557da30db892c06592384ef78b9d81740138"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product is a unified CLI named `vp`; `vp run <agent>` launches an agent with no required configuration, and extra arguments after `--` are forwarded to the agent process."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f7492468b539c503e317b0cef46179c58eb1bd30e2fa892b8f531ba7e47bded3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Individual images can be overridden per agent via environment variables such as `VP_IMAGE_CLAUDE`, plus `VP_DATASETTE_IMAGE` for the dashboard and `VP_SKILLS_ENGINE_IMAGE` for skills commands."}],"claim_ids":["clm_3dbcc01d27a7595931ef4e502a5001acfd59a66f9f972c02f0033bfc42a88a7e","clm_4159193229c12321477102e459493848f58508a800d2f989df15964f27e1c450","clm_5835348860345d9d0d91ce0e68f0d4f6378517660cfe16d6ca8f8bbde6244210","clm_65cc574b85b2d8a5f9efa36f1c855bda2b1ab476aa5abfcf379e73838cbb5b5a","clm_718605621670a3b371a48d654c4c4b2de63b573a603ad07da77607bb1ae4162f","clm_8ebe4a6ab137885c1e9b9ff564cfee3a0418039e0220a972aac6dfa2e0d88600","clm_a5c4ffb79a0645efc9a4f803666364306864eaba630392c31d9710da2edf9363","clm_b6ec1f0db41fcf1a048564c6adca0287e2245852b103ad24e02b9f1a8f76037a","clm_e571f591456707e025b6162ad43133b5cb9107c0f1256c63a64c83faadb4b670","clm_e91eaa48f1a08e42e542895ab9a6557da30db892c06592384ef78b9d81740138","clm_f7492468b539c503e317b0cef46179c58eb1bd30e2fa892b8f531ba7e47bded3"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:21:45Z","created_by_operation":"op_4c9aa1a94916442b9ede63ee46a01d22","id":"pg_c6fef79f1fc75c6dbd8f1230477d47ba","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/vibepod-vibepod-cli-readme-md-ef6519007b1d-1230477d47ba.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_0da32aa802d754e78c8c9e564f0d43e5"],"title":"VibePod/vibepod-cli/README.md @ ef6519007b1d","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:21:45Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4c9aa1a94916442b9ede63ee46a01d22"}
